## Pre-freeze acceptance dependency

#174 must consume the standards-first contract decisions from #390 before it can claim semantic full-stack acceptance.

In addition to the existing runtime/workload gates, #174 should verify that:
- portable intent contains service semantics, not provider products;
- existing v0.4 capability IDs have an explicit compatibility classification;
- Service Binding connection outputs use standard well-known names where applicable;
- Provider Catalog metadata and Runtime Provider Registry state are not conflated;
- provider/version/product/artifact version axes remain independent.
